{
 "_about": "THE AUTHORED ROSTER. Hand-edit this file. No script writes it, ever.",
 "_what_is_here": {
  "families": "the roster: family key -> the checkpoints at each position (base / ego / superego / reinforced_superego / reasoning). Adding a model means adding it HERE and nowhere else.",
  "checkpoints": "per-checkpoint declared facts: org_type, country, scale, open_weight, open_data, and where a position was declared per checkpoint rather than per family, the evidence for it."
 },
 "_the_rule": "AUTHORED vs GENERATED is the distinction this file exists to make. `roster/registry.json` is GENERATED -- this file joined with the measurement artifacts -- and is regenerate-only, because a cache that can outrank its source is how 59 models shadowed 112 for five weeks. That rule is correct and it is WHY declarations ended up in `__init__.py`: there was no authored file for them to live in, and code was the only place a hand edit survived a rebuild. This file is that missing input.",
 "_replaces": [
  "malign_logits/__init__.py MODEL_FAMILIES (64 families, ~600 lines)",
  "data/model_curated.json (59)",
  "data/registry_extra_models.json (8) -- the file named 'extra' because it held 'rows that entered by a path the producer did not know'"
 ],
 "_provenance": "Extracted losslessly 2026-08-15; the loader rebuilds MODEL_FAMILIES field-identical from this file and the round-trip is asserted in tests. RH: 'why can't we have one master json of all information about models?'",
